{"1-5":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2167","lemma":"זָמַר","tr":"za·mar","gloss":"to sing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":45},{"base":"H5782","lemma":"עוּר","tr":"ur","gloss":"to rouse","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":80},{"base":"H3519","lemma":"כָּבוֹד","tr":"ka·vod","gloss":"glory","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":200},{"base":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","tr":"sha·ma·yim","gloss":"heaven","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":421},{"base":"H0523","lemma":"אֻמָּה","tr":"um·mah","gloss":"people","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H7834","lemma":"שַׁ֫חַק","tr":"sha·chaq","gloss":"cloud","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H7837","lemma":"שַׁ֫חַר","tr":"sha·char","gloss":"dawn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H5035","lemma":"נֵ֫בֶל","tr":"ne·vel","gloss":"bag","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":38},{"base":"H3658","lemma":"כִּנּוֹר","tr":"kin·nor","gloss":"lyre","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":42},{"base":"H1077","lemma":"בַּל","tr":"bal","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":73}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":57,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"My heart is steadfast, O God, my heart is steadfast. I will sing and make music.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":57,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"Be exalted, O God, above the heavens; may Your glory cover all the earth.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":145,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"My mouth will declare the praise of the LORD; let every creature bless His holy name forever and ever.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":146,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"I will praise the LORD all my life; I will sing praises to my God while I have my being.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":71,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"My mouth will declare Your righteousness and Your salvation all day long, though I cannot know their full measure.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":104,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"I will sing to the LORD all my life; I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":68,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"God arises. His enemies are scattered, and those who hate Him flee His presence.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":71,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"When I sing praise to You my lips will shout for joy, along with my soul, which You have redeemed.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"6-9":{"people":[{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[{"id":"shechem-h7927g","name":"Shechem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"succoth-h5523g","name":"Succoth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"edom-h0123g","name":"Edom","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"words":[{"base":"H7366","lemma":"רַ֫חַץ","tr":"ra·chats","gloss":"washing","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6429","lemma":"פְּלֶ֫שֶׁת","tr":"pe·le·shet","gloss":"Philistia","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H3039","lemma":"יָדִיד","tr":"ye·did","gloss":"beloved","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":908},{"base":"H5937","lemma":"עָלַז","tr":"a·laz","gloss":"to exult","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H5523","lemma":"סֻכּוֹת","tr":"suk·kot","gloss":"Succoth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H2710","lemma":"חָקַק","tr":"cha·qaq","gloss":"to decree","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"H5275","lemma":"נַ֫עַל","tr":"na·al","gloss":"sandal","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H5518","lemma":"סִיר","tr":"sir","gloss":"pot","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34},{"base":"H4581","lemma":"מָעוֹז","tr":"ma·oz","gloss":"security","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2CH","chapter":32,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"In response, King Hezekiah and the prophet Isaiah son of Amoz cried out to heaven in prayer,","from":6},{"book":"2CH","chapter":32,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"So the LORD saved Hezekiah and the people of Jerusalem from the hands of King Sennacherib of Assyria and all the others, and He gave them rest on every side.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":60,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Respond and save us with Your right hand, that Your beloved may be delivered.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":60,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"With God we will perform with valor, and He will trample our enemies.","from":6},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Concerning Benjamin he said: “May the beloved of the LORD rest secure in Him; God shields him all day long, and upon His shoulders he rests.”","from":6},{"book":"COL","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, clothe yourselves with hearts of compassion, kindness, humility, gentleness, and patience.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":35,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Contend with my opponents, O LORD; fight against those who fight against me.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":35,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Draw the spear and javelin against my pursuers; say to my soul: “I am your salvation.”","from":6}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"10-13":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"edom-h0123g","name":"Edom","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"words":[{"base":"H6862","lemma":"צַר","tr":"tsar","gloss":"narrow","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"H4310","lemma":"מִי","tr":"mi","gloss":"who?","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":423},{"base":"H0947","lemma":"בּוּס","tr":"bus","gloss":"to trample","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H2986","lemma":"יָבַל","tr":"ya·val","gloss":"to conduct","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H2186","lemma":"זָנַח","tr":"za·nach","gloss":"to reject","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H5833","lemma":"עֶזְרָה","tr":"ez·rah","gloss":"help","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":26},{"base":"H3051","lemma":"יָהַב","tr":"ya·hav","gloss":"to give","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":33},{"base":"H8668","lemma":"תְּשׁוּעָה","tr":"te·shu·ah","gloss":"deliverance: salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34},{"base":"H4013","lemma":"מִבְצָר","tr":"miv·tsar","gloss":"fortification","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":37},{"base":"H5148","lemma":"נָחָה","tr":"na·chah","gloss":"to lead","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":118,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD is on my side; I will not be afraid. What can man do to me?","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":118,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"I was pushed so hard I was falling, but the LORD helped me.","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":60,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"With God we will perform with valor, and He will trample our enemies.","from":13},{"book":"JER","chapter":17,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"This is what the LORD says: “Cursed is the man who trusts in mankind, who makes mere flesh his strength and turns his heart from the LORD.","from":12},{"book":"JER","chapter":17,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"He is like a tree planted by the waters that sends out its roots toward the stream. It does not fear when the heat comes, and its leaves are always green. It does not worry in a year of drought, nor does it cease to produce fruit.","from":12},{"book":"NUM","chapter":10,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When you enter into battle in your land against an adversary who attacks you, sound short blasts on the trumpets, and you will be remembered before the LORD your God and saved from your enemies.","from":11},{"book":"DEU","chapter":20,"verse":3,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"saying to them, “Hear, O Israel, today you are going into battle with your enemies. Do not be fainthearted or afraid; do not be alarmed or terrified because of them. For the LORD your God goes with you to fight for you against your enemies, to give you the victory.”","from":11},{"book":"JDG","chapter":15,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And he struck them ruthlessly with a great slaughter, and then went down and stayed in the cave at the rock of Etam.","from":13}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}